Analyze analyst ratings changes for S&P 500 companies published this week. Identify companies with significant rating upgrades or downgrades and assess their potential impact on the index. Consider the credibility of the analysts (track record) and the size of the affected companies. Use that information as one layer to a prediction of what the other layers (macro) will do to the price on the remaining trading days. Calculate an expected price change based on the rating changes and adjust the sentiment accordingly. Increase conviction if the analysis consensus on rating changes shows strong disagreement.